              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for a compass, then the Russian for a satnav."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: указатель",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "указатель (ukazátel) — \"a signpost; an index\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "По указателю до озера три километра. Po ukazátelyu do ózera tri kilométra. According to the signpost it is three kilometres to the lake."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. Дорожный указатель (ukazátel) — a road sign."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "указатель (ukazátel) is built on указать 'to show the way' with -тель, from казать 'to show', the root of сказать 'to say'. EtymDB lists указатель (ukazátel) without a deeper source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
